      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence shows the authors report that Twitter data makes better predictions about language inventory (fewer missing languages, fewer false negatives) and offer hypotheses/explanations. The Discussion attributes differences to Twitter representing different, more wealthy/urban populations (better match with GDP-weighted populations), and the Language Identification section suggests datasets dominated by widely used languages with a fixed 100k-word threshold bias representation. Thus the authors do offer explanatory hypotheses, though for the missing-language advantage they primarily describe the pattern and attribute it to data-collection biases rather than giving a single crisp causal hypothesis."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 4872.071499936283
